{"chunk_id": "2cd2aca8fc99", "text": "This chapter recounts the origin story of Vedavati and its hidden link to Sita and Ravana\u2019s eventual downfall. After receiving the divine sword Chandrahasa and extended life from Shiva, Ravana roams the world conquering kings. In the Himalayas he encounters Vedavati, a radiant ascetic princess performing severe penance to marry Vishnu, fulfilling her slain father\u2019s wish. Ravana mocks her devotion and tries to seduce her, boasting of his own power. When she rebukes him and praises Vishnu, Ravana seizes her hair. In fury and defilement, Vedavati cuts off her hair, declares that she will be reborn to destroy him, and enters a sacred fire. The narrative reveals that she is later reborn as Janaka\u2019s daughter\u2014Sita\u2014whose fate ultimately leads to Ravana\u2019s destruction.\nRavana encounters the ascetic Vedavati, who rejects him, curses his destruction, immolates herself, and is later reborn as Sita to bring about his downfall.\nThemes: destiny and rebirth, chastity and devotion, arrogance of Ravana, divine justice, curse and prophecy", "vector": [-0.0013283443404361606, -0.033782873302698135, 0.003689201083034277, 0.0102754021063447, -0.010812374763190746, 0.01277464535087347, -0.03481703996658325, -0.016135696321725845, -0.02577468752861023, -0.013019929639995098, 0.03150239586830139, 0.01921168901026249, 0.024833327159285545, 0.010050006210803986, -0.006125465966761112, -0.00898269098252058, 0.038980238139629364, -0.022247903048992157, 0.028824161738157272, -0.022353973239660263, 0.0034770637284964323, -0.016639523208141327, -0.009871015325188637, 0.016772108152508736, -0.026689529418945312, -0.002355055883526802, 0.021584974601864815, -0.033756352961063385, 0.017925605177879333, -0.012290706858038902, -0.02500568889081478, -0.005850350018590689, -0.0050912960432469845, -0.011820027604699135, -0.018495725467801094, 0.005217252764850855, -0.007703237235546112, -0.018707862123847008, -0.0020252487156540155, -2.6